/surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Stotz-Potter</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Monroe</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Morin</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of the dorsomedial hypothalamus in the cardiovascular response to stress</article-title><source>Clinical and Experimental Pharmacology and Physiology</source><year>1996</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>171</fpage><lpage>176</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8819648</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stotz-Potter</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name><name><surname>DiMicco</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Muscimol acts in dorsomedial but not paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus to suppress cardiovascular effects of stress</article-title><source>J Neurosci</source><year>1996</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>1173</fpage><lpage>1179</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8558246</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rostrup</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekeberg</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Awareness of high blood pressure influences on psychological and sympathetic responses</article-title><source>J Psychosom Res</source><year>1992</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>117</fpage><lpage>123</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1560424</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0022-3999(92)90020-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rostrup</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mundal</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Westheim</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Eide</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Awareness of high blood pressure increases arterial plasma catecholamines, platelet noradrenaline and adrenergic responses to mental stress</article-title><source>J Hypertens</source><year>1991</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>166</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1849532</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00004872-199102000-00010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Peuler</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Simultaneous single isotope radioenzymatic assay of plasma norepinephrine, epinephrine and dopamine</article-title><source>Life Sci</source><year>1977</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>625</fpage><lpage>636</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">904439</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0024-3205(77)90070-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kjeldsen</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Flaaten</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Eide</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Helgeland</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Leren</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence of increased peripheral catecholamine release in patients with long-standing, untreated essential hypertension</article-title><source>Scand J Clin Lab Invest</source><year>1982</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>223</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7134805</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wikl